{
  "statement": "Measured on the cast: seven people with real threads, conversations, notes and memories in a database of their own, read through the same queries the worker runs. Memories are learned from their own words only, never from a shared thread, an email or a forgotten memory, never the sensitive list unasked; filing keeps their words in a shared thread; asking shows them; forgetting finds them.",
  "why": "A fixture describes a context; the cast is one, built the way the database builds it, so a filter, a grant or a bound that is wrong shows up here and nowhere else. When an edge case turns up, it is added to cast.sql for the person it would happen to, and here.",
  "sources": [
    "038 feature-spec",
    "cast/README.md",
    "cast/cast.sql"
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "behrooz-pass",
      "why": "a friend stated in passing and a shorthand are learned; a forgotten memory's words and a move he only might make are not",
      "surface": "cast-memory",
      "input": {
        "character": "behrooz"
      },
      "expect": {
        "has": [
          "Sam"
        ],
        "lacks": [
          "Corolla",
          "Montreal"
        ],
        "never_touches": [
          "0ca50000-0000-4000-8004-000000000112",
          "0ca50000-0000-4000-8004-000000000111"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "meera-pass",
      "why": "her sister is learned; a forwarded email's 'remember' never is, and nor is being exhausted",
      "surface": "cast-memory",
      "input": {
        "character": "meera"
      },
      "expect": {
        "has": [
          "Rina"
        ],
        "lacks": [
          "PIN",
          "4432",
          "exhausted",
          "approved"
        ],
        "never_touches": [
          "0ca50000-0000-4000-8004-000000000211"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sam-pass",
      "why": "a day of bike errands holds nothing about Sam",
